NUM-29: average an N = 0 subarea's runoff over the whole step

A subarea with Manning's n = 0 releases its ponded depth in excess of
depression storage within the step. In the step in which depression storage
fills, RunoffSolver::execute() turned that excess into a rate by dividing by
t_runoff, the time left after storage filled, while Voutflow and the
subcatchment runoff book the rate over the full step dt. The water that
had just filled depression storage was therefore also counted as runoff.
Divide by dt instead, so that rate x dt is the excess volume (the same
change as the 5.3.0 patch).

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-29_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp b/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp
index aa81dc7..a82a910 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp
@@ -520,7 +520,10 @@ void RunoffSolver::execute(SimulationContext& ctx, double dt, double evap_rate_i
                     if (subarea_n > 0.0) {
                         runoff_rate = alpha * std::pow(xDepth, MEXP);
                     } else {
-                        runoff_rate = xDepth / t_runoff;
+                        // averaged over the full step dt, not over the
+                        // time t_runoff after depression storage filled:
+                        // Voutflow books it over dt
+                        runoff_rate = xDepth / dt;
                         depth = dStore;
                     }
                 }
